Number of Exits
Roll 1d6 to determine the number of exits for the
room or chamber.
1 - There is only one exit (back the way
you came). The room is seemingly a
dead end.
2 to 5 - There are 2 exits inclusive of the
point of entry.
6 - There are 3 exits inclusive to the point
of entry.
A dead end room may be searched for a single
secret door. For each 10 feet searched, there is
a 1-in-12 chance of discovering a secret door.
Neither the floor nor ceiling may be searched in
this manner.
