There is a 1-in-100 chance that a stairway goes
both up and down. Otherwise, there is an even
chance that a stairway goes up or down.
Dungeon levels are separated by 20 to 30 feet of
earth or stone.
There is a 1-in-10 chance that the stairway
spirals. All of these should be indicated by a
circular chamber 20 feet in diameter. Otherwise,
the stairway is represented by a 5' wide and 10'
long (more or less).
Stairway - Direction and Distance
For each stairway where the direction and
distance is unknown* roll 1d8. This decides the
direction from the center of the map. The
stairway can fall anywhere within one of these 45
degree arcs. Exactly where within the arc can be
randomized, once the distance is determined (see
below).
1 - North
2 - Northeast
3 - East
4 - Southeast
5 - South
6 - Southwest
7 - West
8 - Northwest
* The direction and distance of some stairways
may have already been determined by another
dungeon level which already connects to the
current level which is being generated.
Next, roll 2d6 to find the approximate distance
from the center of the map. Finally, 1d5 (half of
a ten-sided dice roll) can be used to find the exact
distance within a particular 50 foot band.
